{
 "id": "2026-10-25-rotation-eigenvalues",
 "topic": "complex eigenvalues of a rotation",
 "subject": "math",
 "hook_type": "myth bust",
 "caption": "A 90° rotation knocks every real vector off its span, so it has no real eigenvectors. Compute anyway and you get λ = ±i, and multiplying by i is itself a quarter turn. Imaginary eigenvalues are the signature of rotation.\n\nSave this for your linear algebra course.\n\n#linearalgebra #eigenvalues #complexnumbers #math #mathematics #stem #engineering #physics #machinelearning",
 "cover_at": 1.0,
 "hook": "Here's a matrix with no eigenvectors. At least, no real ones.",
 "beats": [
  {
   "text": "This matrix rotates every vector by ninety degrees.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "plane",
     "name": "P",
     "range": [
      -3,
      3
     ],
     "at": [
      0,
      0.4
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "A",
     "tex": "A=\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}",
     "size": 68,
     "at": "top"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Remember, an eigenvector stays on its own span. It just gets stretched or squished.",
   "do": [
    {
     "sfx": "tick"
    },
    {
     "together": [
      {
       "make": "vector",
       "name": "v1",
       "on": "P",
       "to": [
        1,
        0.5
       ],
       "color": "blue"
      },
      {
       "make": "vector",
       "name": "v2",
       "on": "P",
       "to": [
        -0.5,
        1
       ],
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "make": "vector",
       "name": "v3",
       "on": "P",
       "to": [
        1,
        -1
       ],
       "color": "teal"
      },
      {
       "make": "vector",
       "name": "v4",
       "on": "P",
       "to": [
        0.4,
        1.2
       ],
       "color": "brown"
      }
     ],
     "lag": 0.2
    },
    {
     "together": [
      {
       "make": "span",
       "on": "P",
       "dir": [
        1,
        0.5
       ],
       "color": "blue"
      },
      {
       "make": "span",
       "on": "P",
       "dir": [
        -0.5,
        1
       ],
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "make": "span",
       "on": "P",
       "dir": [
        1,
        -1
       ],
       "color": "teal"
      },
      {
       "make": "span",
       "on": "P",
       "dir": [
        0.4,
        1.2
       ],
       "color": "brown"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "But under a rotation, every vector gets knocked off its span. Not one survives.",
   "do": [
    {
     "apply_matrix": [
      [
       0,
       -1
      ],
      [
       1,
       0
      ]
     ],
     "to": [
      "v1",
      "v2",
      "v3",
      "v4"
     ],
     "on": "P"
    },
    {
     "sfx": "thud"
    },
    {
     "indicate": [
      "v1",
      "v2",
      "v3",
      "v4"
     ],
     "color": "red"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "clear": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "And yet, if you dutifully compute the eigenvalues anyway...",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "e1",
     "tex": "\\det(A - \\lambda I) = 0",
     "size": 92,
     "at": [
      0,
      3.6
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "e2",
     "tex": "\\lambda^2 + 1 = 0",
     "size": 92,
     "next_to": "e1",
     "buff": 0.9
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "you find $\\lambda^2 = -1$. So $\\lambda = i$ or $\\lambda = -i$.",
   "do": [
    {
     "sfx": "riser"
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "e3",
     "tex": [
      "\\lambda = i",
      "\\quad\\text{or}\\quad",
      "\\lambda = -i"
     ],
     "size": 84,
     "colors": {
      "0": "yellow",
      "2": "yellow"
     },
     "next_to": "e2",
     "buff": 0.9
    },
    {
     "sfx": "ding"
    },
    {
     "make": "box",
     "name": "b",
     "around": "e3"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "group",
     "name": "eqs",
     "of": [
      "e1",
      "e2",
      "e3"
     ]
    },
    {
     "together": [
      {
       "hide": "b"
      },
      {
       "move": "eqs",
       "to": [
        0,
        4.9
       ],
       "scale": 0.55
      }
     ],
     "time": 0.6
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Is the algebra just giving nonsense? Not at all. Multiplying by $i$ is itself a quarter turn.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "plane",
     "name": "C",
     "complex": true,
     "range": [
      -2,
      2
     ],
     "size": 6.6,
     "at": [
      0,
      0
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "one",
     "tex": "1",
     "size": 68,
     "on": "C",
     "at": [
      1.15,
      -0.25
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "vector",
     "name": "z",
     "on": "C",
     "to": [
      1,
      0
     ],
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 10
    },
    {
     "sfx": "whoosh"
    },
    {
     "together": [
      {
       "rotate": "z",
       "angle": 90,
       "on": "C"
      },
      {
       "make": "shape",
       "kind": "arc",
       "on": "C",
       "radius": 1,
       "start": 0,
       "angle": 90,
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "make": "tex",
       "name": "ii",
       "tex": "i",
       "size": 68,
       "color": "yellow",
       "on": "C",
       "at": [
        -0.25,
        1.15
       ]
      },
      {
       "make": "tex",
       "name": "xi",
       "tex": "\\times i",
       "size": 80,
       "color": "yellow",
       "on": "C",
       "at": [
        1.2,
        1.2
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "sfx": "ding"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "So the algebra was telling you something real. The scaling factor is a rotation.",
   "do": [
    {
     "indicate": "e3",
     "color": "yellow"
    },
    {
     "indicate": "xi",
     "scale": 1.3
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "clear": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "In general, imaginary eigenvalues are the signature of some kind of rotation.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "text",
     "name": "r1",
     "text": "imaginary eigenvalues",
     "size": 70,
     "color": "yellow",
